  "question": {
    "text": "Nitrogen gas is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> temperature. The temperature (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> ) at which the rms speed of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> molecule would be equal to the rms speed of a nitrogen molecule, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>28</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ).<br />&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "41",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p></blockquote><p>Temperature of Nitrogen gas is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>573</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>Molar mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p>Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p>The rms speed of gas is given by</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Now rms speed of hydrogen gas is equal to rms speed of nitrogen gas, i.e.;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mfenced><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mfenced><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Substitute the given values i above equation, we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>28</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>573</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>41</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p>"
  }
}